# Disassembly work

Skill descriptions are not loaded on their own. Before any edit to `*.asm`,
`*.blocks`, `ram.inc`, `workbench.cfg`, or `docs/progress.md` / `docs/game-notes.md`,
Read these and follow them:

1. `tools/workbench/skills/konami-msx-disasm/SKILL.md`
2. `tools/workbench/skills/msx-code-data/SKILL.md`
3. `tools/workbench/skills/msx-regen/SKILL.md` when regenerating or folding a bank
4. `tools/workbench/skills/msx-romscan/SKILL.md` when searching for callers or tables
5. `docs/progress.md` and `docs/game-notes.md`
6. Every `SKILL.md` under `.agents/skills/`

Game notes win on this ROM's addresses. Workbench skills stay generic.
`make verify` after every edit.

Read `msx-gfx`, `msx-gfx-sheets`, `msx-psg-catalogue`, `konami-psg`, or
`msx-cocoamsx` when the task is graphics, sound, or tracing. Not on a naming pass.

```
# Bad: fold the next bank from memory of the pager.
# Good: Read konami-msx-disasm, then name the resident window before that fold.
```
